WEBVTT

00:48.715 --> 00:50.258
EMERGENCY

01:04.439 --> 01:06.066
Hello. This is Team Two.

01:06.900 --> 01:08.151
Yes. Why?

01:09.694 --> 01:11.696
What? An accident?

01:16.534 --> 01:18.787
"Accident"? What accident?

01:20.246 --> 01:22.165
Did someone get hurt?

01:29.422 --> 01:30.715
Turn it around.

01:34.552 --> 01:35.678
Hurry, hurry.

01:36.554 --> 01:38.306
Doctor! Doctor!

01:38.389 --> 01:40.100
It's critical.

01:41.351 --> 01:42.769
Healthy, late 20s, male.

01:42.852 --> 01:46.189
Injured in an explosive blast,
unable to open his eyes.

01:46.272 --> 01:48.191
100 over 60, 120bpm.

01:48.274 --> 01:49.901
- Treatment room. Go now.
- Yes, sir.

01:52.070 --> 01:54.155
- Does this patient have a guardian?
- I'm here.

01:54.239 --> 01:55.365
I'm here for him.

01:55.865 --> 01:57.575
Can I get his family and first name?

01:57.659 --> 02:01.121
Lee Si-woo. He's with the KMA.

02:05.125 --> 02:06.501
Who's hurt?

02:07.544 --> 02:08.711
It's Mr. Lee.

02:14.551 --> 02:16.344
The hospital says he's very hurt.

02:25.145 --> 02:26.896
You should go, Forecaster Lee.

02:31.568 --> 02:32.610
I have to go where?

02:32.694 --> 02:34.362
The Jeju Typhoon Center.

02:34.445 --> 02:35.488
You're a good fit.

02:39.909 --> 02:41.077
Are you kidding me?

02:41.786 --> 02:44.247
All the decisions I make at work
are taken seriously.

02:46.666 --> 02:50.295
So that means
you've given this considerable thought.

02:52.088 --> 02:54.632
Mm-hmm. If you're okay with it.

02:58.094 --> 03:00.555
If the body temperature drops
about one degree,

03:00.638 --> 03:03.892
its level of immunity
becomes 30 percent weaker.

03:05.977 --> 03:08.938
Ha-kyung doesn't date just anybody
unless there's a chance of marriage.

03:10.231 --> 03:11.858
You are aware of that, right?

03:12.358 --> 03:17.238
That means it becomes that much
more vulnerable to external threats.

03:20.033 --> 03:21.117
What are you…

03:21.993 --> 03:23.286
What's this about?

03:23.369 --> 03:25.121
We both need space.

03:25.788 --> 03:27.790
I think it's important for both of us.

03:28.833 --> 03:29.959
Yu-jin.

03:30.043 --> 03:34.088
We should take some time to think
how we can make this work.

03:36.049 --> 03:38.384
You know you need it as much as I do.

03:46.100 --> 03:50.230
We do have some time still,
so you can let me know.

03:51.606 --> 03:53.775
Uh, no.

03:54.984 --> 03:56.027
I'll do it.

03:56.694 --> 03:58.112
You should give it more thought.

03:58.196 --> 04:02.116
There's nothing to go over now.
Like you said, it's official business.

04:02.200 --> 04:03.993
I'll go.

04:09.499 --> 04:10.708
It's settled.

04:14.837 --> 04:16.881
Anything you want to say?

04:16.965 --> 04:18.299
Oh, no.

04:22.887 --> 04:24.138
Okay.

04:32.814 --> 04:35.650
The same goes
for the temperature between two people.

04:40.863 --> 04:44.158
If you leave me right now,
then that's it for us.

04:46.244 --> 04:47.662
Have you thought carefully about this?

04:52.250 --> 04:53.668
If that's what you want…

04:54.961 --> 04:56.170
well, okay.

05:15.898 --> 05:18.985
The 77-4 bus will be arriving shortly.

05:49.015 --> 05:51.351
One tiny thing
someone says to you,

05:51.434 --> 05:57.357
one small twitch of their face
can sometimes turn your emotions ice-cold.

05:59.859 --> 06:00.985
And…

06:04.030 --> 06:05.198
Oh, no.

06:07.325 --> 06:09.744
There was an accident?
Where? Where and how bad was it?

06:10.370 --> 06:12.955
Ho… hold on a moment. Who is this?

06:13.039 --> 06:14.832
If you tell me
which hospital it is, I'll--

06:14.916 --> 06:17.668
This is Chae Yu-jin.

06:25.176 --> 06:27.303
I'm with Si-woo right now.

06:28.304 --> 06:32.517
When your emotional temperature
drops even one degree,

06:33.142 --> 06:39.315
you become highly sensitive,
vulnerable to the outside environment.

06:53.162 --> 06:57.583
EPISODE 11
1

06:58.418 --> 07:00.211
2 DAYS AGO

07:49.802 --> 07:52.638
Watch out for signs
of physical and mental exhaustion

07:52.722 --> 07:54.223
as the hot weather continues.

07:54.307 --> 07:57.685
Heat wave advisories have been issued
in the Yeongnam area

07:57.768 --> 07:59.562
and most of the western region.

07:59.645 --> 08:02.482
And the heat wave warning
has been issued in Gwangju.

08:05.818 --> 08:07.195
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

08:07.945 --> 08:10.573
Ah, hell. No sign of rain yet, Director?

08:10.656 --> 08:14.577
There will be a light rain under 5mm
from the wind on the east coast.

08:14.660 --> 08:16.704
However, it will only reach Gangwon.

08:17.288 --> 08:20.291
That doesn't even count as rain, really.

08:20.958 --> 08:22.418
Wow, red across the board.

08:22.502 --> 08:25.004
The Ministry of the Interior and Safety
is going on the news

08:25.087 --> 08:26.672
to announce some safety measures today.

08:26.756 --> 08:30.343
Local governments have agreed
to try and set up heat shelter facilities.

08:30.426 --> 08:32.595
Okay.

08:32.678 --> 08:35.056
A lot of government offices
are gonna get hit hard, huh?

08:35.139 --> 08:36.390
It's inevitable.

08:36.474 --> 08:38.184
What shall we do this weekend?

08:38.267 --> 08:39.936
It's the last one before I leave for Jeju.

08:40.520 --> 08:42.021
What are you doing?

08:42.605 --> 08:43.814
What's wrong?

08:45.858 --> 08:46.901
What? Go ahead.

08:47.568 --> 08:48.611
Uh, yes, sir.

08:48.694 --> 08:51.239
Let's start with impact forecast
for each region affected.

08:52.698 --> 08:54.700
How about
duck baeksuk in Gapyeong?

08:55.284 --> 08:57.161
Duck baeksuk in Gapyeong--

08:57.245 --> 08:58.204
Hmm?

09:05.545 --> 09:07.004
I apologize.

09:07.088 --> 09:10.091
Uh, I think that an emphasis
on water temperature control

09:10.174 --> 09:12.718
and shading near fish farms
would be appropriate.

09:13.803 --> 09:17.807
Oh, and let's remind the press
to restrain from their catastrophizing.

09:17.890 --> 09:19.267
We'll do our best, Director.

09:19.350 --> 09:20.351
Thanks.

09:20.851 --> 09:23.104
If there's nothing further,
we'll adjourn this meeting.

09:23.187 --> 09:25.022
- Good work, all.
- Great work.

09:25.106 --> 09:26.399
- Great job.
- Thank you.

09:26.482 --> 09:29.110
Duck baeksuk in Gapyeong
sounds pretty good.

09:29.193 --> 09:32.154
Oh, right.
Did you make your decision?

09:33.531 --> 09:36.158
- The typhoon center, who's going?
- Uh, yes.

09:36.701 --> 09:39.579
- It's typhoon season already?
- Yeah, someone's gotta go.

09:39.662 --> 09:41.247
Well, who is it, huh?

09:41.330 --> 09:43.499
You don't think it could be me, do you?

09:47.253 --> 09:48.462
What? You haven't decided yet?

09:51.299 --> 09:52.633
I'm going, sir. It's me.

09:54.552 --> 09:56.929
Huh? It's you? Since when?

09:57.013 --> 09:59.015
Yesterday.

09:59.098 --> 10:00.391
- Oh!
- Congratulations.

10:00.474 --> 10:02.435
- Congrats.
- Okay, then.

10:02.518 --> 10:04.854
Forecaster Lee and Director Jin,
I'll see you in my office.

10:04.937 --> 10:06.105
Yes, sir.

10:11.027 --> 10:13.487
Oh, Bo-mi. Hey.

10:15.197 --> 10:16.699
Oh, okay.

10:17.241 --> 10:19.160
I wish I could go to Jeju.

10:20.328 --> 10:21.871
You seem
so excited to go to Jeju.

10:21.954 --> 10:24.915
I'm not excited about Jeju.
I'm excited about the typhoon center.

10:24.999 --> 10:26.834
I've always wanted to work there.

10:26.917 --> 10:29.128
You know me. I love field work.

10:29.211 --> 10:31.422
You told me that Headquarters
was your dream.

10:31.505 --> 10:33.174
Now you're saying you prefer the field?

10:33.257 --> 10:35.468
What can I say? I'm multi-talented.

10:36.761 --> 10:39.430
Good for you and, uh, best of luck.

10:39.513 --> 10:42.433
What's wrong?
You're the one that told me to go.

10:44.185 --> 10:47.104
Anyway, I don't like
the duck baeksuk in Gapyeong idea.

11:14.423 --> 11:17.718
We will now begin the briefing
for the 29th of July.

11:18.302 --> 11:21.389
Currently in Korea, the lower atmosphere
is filled with hot and humid air,

11:21.472 --> 11:24.350
and the upper atmosphere
is filled with hot and dry air.

11:24.975 --> 11:26.143
The cause of this heat wave

11:26.227 --> 11:29.563
is the North Pacific anticyclone
which has expanded to the south

11:29.647 --> 11:33.275
and also the Tibetan anticyclone
from inland China heading westward.

11:42.743 --> 11:45.788
ELECTRONIC CIVIL SERVICE CENTER
DIVORCE

11:51.627 --> 11:53.713
PETITION FOR DIVORCE

12:22.074 --> 12:23.617
Boo!

12:23.701 --> 12:25.202
What are you doing?

12:25.286 --> 12:29.165
I thought I wouldn't see you here.

12:29.248 --> 12:31.041
I told you my school trip
has one more day here.

12:31.125 --> 12:32.376
So when's it done?

12:32.460 --> 12:35.087
The last part's the weather chart
listing in ten minutes.

12:35.171 --> 12:37.965
So we could have, uh, a bite soon, yeah?

12:38.048 --> 12:39.967
The food at the cafeteria here
is really good.

12:40.050 --> 12:41.051
Hmm…

12:42.219 --> 12:43.053
Well, okay.

12:45.848 --> 12:47.057
What time should I be there?

12:47.141 --> 12:49.143
Ah, you just call me, okay?

12:49.226 --> 12:50.603
After class, yeah?

12:50.686 --> 12:51.771
Okay.

12:53.439 --> 12:55.107
Tomorrow?

12:55.191 --> 12:56.358
Mm-hmm.

12:57.693 --> 12:59.653
- Why? Should he not?
- It's too soon, sir.

12:59.737 --> 13:01.322
I thought we'd have the whole week.

13:01.405 --> 13:04.658
You know Director Sung
at the typhoon center. She's impatient.

13:05.534 --> 13:06.911
All week, she's been bugging me

13:06.994 --> 13:09.580
about when we're gonna send her
our forecaster.

13:10.164 --> 13:11.290
She says they should come ASAP

13:11.373 --> 13:13.834
to get acquainted
with the station practices,

13:14.585 --> 13:16.545
to avoid any mistakes
when the typhoons really start.

13:16.629 --> 13:17.880
What could I say?

13:17.963 --> 13:20.674
I get her concerns.
But we have our own problems here.

13:20.758 --> 13:23.552
You know it's crazy
because of the heat wave right now.

13:24.386 --> 13:28.098
Couldn't he continue covering
all of that from down there? Huh?

13:28.849 --> 13:30.476
- Uh…
- And aside from the heat,

13:30.559 --> 13:32.978
I only told him
he's going to Jeju yesterday.

13:33.562 --> 13:35.523
- He needs time to prepare.
- No, it's fine.

13:37.483 --> 13:38.776
He says it's fine, see?

13:38.859 --> 13:41.987
Yeah. Of course, I can cover
the heat wave from Jeju.

13:42.071 --> 13:43.405
It's really not a problem.

13:43.489 --> 13:45.074
Okay! Great, then.

13:45.658 --> 13:47.743
If that's really all,
he'll go this weekend.

13:47.827 --> 13:50.162
All right. Dismissed.

13:51.038 --> 13:52.373
Jeez.

14:03.008 --> 14:05.261
You can't just say yes so impulsively.

14:05.344 --> 14:07.763
How are you gonna leave tomorrow?
You're not ready to go.

14:07.847 --> 14:10.224
You didn't even want to go to Gapyeong
for duck baeksuk.

14:10.307 --> 14:12.059
I don't have any weekend plans,

14:12.142 --> 14:14.687
so I might as well go
to the typhoon center and work.

14:15.437 --> 14:17.147
Are you serious or just making a scene?

14:17.231 --> 14:19.191
Mm, half and half.

14:20.568 --> 14:22.695
Regardless. We can talk to him again.

14:23.404 --> 14:24.780
Why are you flip-flopping?

14:24.864 --> 14:26.949
This is also confusing now.

14:30.160 --> 14:31.161
What do you mean?

14:31.245 --> 14:34.415
Didn't you want some time for yourself,
away from me?

14:35.749 --> 14:38.335
Isn't that why you wanted me
to go to Jeju?

14:38.961 --> 14:42.214
Then how come you're mad
that I would leave a few days earlier?

14:46.427 --> 14:48.262
I think you're mistaken about something.

14:48.345 --> 14:52.099
I don't ever let my own feelings get
in the way of official weather business.

14:52.182 --> 14:55.394
Even in other relationships,
not once did I do that.

14:59.023 --> 15:01.859
There's no need for us
to talk to the General Director.

15:01.942 --> 15:05.487
I'll just head out tomorrow, Director.

15:26.967 --> 15:28.677
- Reporter Cho.
- Yes?

15:28.761 --> 15:31.055
Is Reporter Chae not here
for the briefing?

15:31.805 --> 15:35.100
Uh… Oh, uh, I heard she took time off.

15:35.184 --> 15:36.560
You haven't heard?

15:36.644 --> 15:39.772
Ah! So that was today.

15:40.481 --> 15:41.523
Yes.

15:41.607 --> 15:44.818
I, uh, forgot when she was… Yeah.

15:44.902 --> 15:46.862
- Right. Goodbye. See you.
- Okay, see you.

16:03.462 --> 16:06.340
WEATHER

16:15.766 --> 16:18.018
KI-JUN

16:28.696 --> 16:29.530
You took time off?

16:32.199 --> 16:34.535
Seriously? Where are you right now?

16:35.244 --> 16:37.788
Come back home. We need to talk in person.

16:46.338 --> 16:49.800
FLIGHT RESERVATION

16:52.261 --> 16:54.471
FROM SEOUL TO JEJU ISLAND

16:54.555 --> 16:56.932
BOOK A FLIGHT

17:13.365 --> 17:14.491
Yu-jin.

17:47.816 --> 17:50.152
What's up?
The vibe is off here.

17:52.821 --> 17:55.991
I think something went down
between the Director and Forecaster Lee

17:56.075 --> 17:57.618
about the typhoon center.

17:57.701 --> 17:59.244
You should do something, Mrs. Oh.

17:59.328 --> 18:01.413
- I should?
- Huh?

18:04.541 --> 18:06.752
You have something to say, Ms. Oh?

18:06.835 --> 18:07.753
Uh, do I?

18:09.797 --> 18:12.341
Uh, it's…

18:13.425 --> 18:14.760
Director…

18:15.677 --> 18:17.763
So should we go for dinner later?

18:21.850 --> 18:23.060
Wait, dinner?

18:23.769 --> 18:25.312
Uh, well…

18:25.395 --> 18:27.064
Forecaster Lee is going to Jeju,

18:27.147 --> 18:31.568
and of course he'll come back soon
since it's just a temporary dispatch.

18:32.152 --> 18:33.278
But still, it would be nice

18:33.362 --> 18:35.614
to have dinner together
and wish him luck before he leaves.

18:36.198 --> 18:37.282
What do you say?

18:37.366 --> 18:38.242
Sounds great.

18:38.826 --> 18:39.868
Oh.

18:39.952 --> 18:42.830
Yeah, sure. Sounds great.

18:42.913 --> 18:44.957
Mr. Shin, what do you say?

18:45.040 --> 18:47.042
- I already have plans.
- Ah.

18:47.626 --> 18:49.044
Could you reschedule?

18:49.670 --> 18:51.964
It's the first Team Two dinner altogether.

18:52.506 --> 18:54.716
Oh, that's true, though.
It'd be the first time.

18:54.800 --> 18:57.094
We've never done that before
with this crew.

18:57.177 --> 19:00.722
Well, it'd be great if you rescheduled,
Mr. Shin, to be with our team.

19:00.806 --> 19:02.224
I really shouldn't. It's important.

19:02.850 --> 19:04.101
I'm sorry.

19:04.685 --> 19:07.855
Oh, well, I suppose it is what it is.

19:08.480 --> 19:09.940
Let's do it.

19:10.023 --> 19:11.275
Huh?

19:11.942 --> 19:14.319
We should have a dinner
whoever can make it.

19:15.070 --> 19:16.405
What do you say, Forecaster?

19:18.782 --> 19:19.700
Yeah.

19:21.952 --> 19:24.538
Well, okay, then.
I'll, uh, get us a reservation.

19:54.985 --> 19:58.030
What's wrong?
This entire dinner thing is just for you.

20:03.118 --> 20:04.995
Why are you upset right now?

20:06.580 --> 20:07.748
"Right now"?

20:08.832 --> 20:11.460
I've never said I'm upset before,
so why would you say "right now"?

20:13.086 --> 20:15.631
I've never once told you I'm upset

20:15.714 --> 20:17.841
since the moment you said
I should go to Jeju.

20:18.592 --> 20:21.178
- What's wrong with you, kid?
- I'm not a kid.

20:21.261 --> 20:22.596
I'm a man.

20:22.679 --> 20:24.139
And in fact, I'm yours.

20:41.281 --> 20:43.033
Hey. Enjoy your lunch.

20:43.116 --> 20:45.077
- Oh, hello.
- Hey.

20:45.160 --> 20:46.787
- Who is this?
- My daughter.

20:46.870 --> 20:49.289
- Oh, your daughter? Go ahead. Here.
- Please go ahead. Go.

20:49.373 --> 20:51.625
- Sure, thanks.
- Adorable.

20:52.626 --> 20:54.503
She's here for her school.

20:54.586 --> 20:56.255
Oh, she's so pretty.

20:56.338 --> 20:58.090
- Right? Yup, she is.
- Uh-huh.

20:59.633 --> 21:04.179
Ah! Here at the, uh, KMA,
the forecasters have the most work,

21:04.263 --> 21:07.474
so, uh, the… the others all know that,

21:07.557 --> 21:10.560
so most of the time,
they'll let us eat first at lunch.

21:11.645 --> 21:13.522
- Thank you. Oh, that's great.
- Here.

21:17.526 --> 21:18.860
Have some vegetables.

21:22.489 --> 21:24.283
Oh, they got sausage.

21:25.117 --> 21:27.869
When I was a kid,
I had this all the time.

21:28.578 --> 21:30.455
It's really good.

21:34.042 --> 21:36.795
Mm, yeah. Mm.

21:36.878 --> 21:38.672
Can we join you for lunch?

21:38.755 --> 21:40.590
- Yeah, sure. Here.
- Oh, of course.

21:40.674 --> 21:42.926
- Slide in right here.
- Oh, thanks.

21:43.552 --> 21:45.387
This is my daughter, Um Bo-mi.

21:45.470 --> 21:46.847
Ah, Um Bo-mi, huh?

21:46.930 --> 21:49.224
- Hello.
- Hello.

21:49.308 --> 21:52.185
These are some of the people
who work with me on the team.

21:53.103 --> 21:54.187
Hello.

21:54.271 --> 21:55.439
- Aw.
- Hello.

21:55.522 --> 21:57.566
- She's beautiful.
- Right?

21:57.649 --> 21:59.192
I guess she takes after her mom.

21:59.276 --> 22:00.569
What are you saying?

22:00.652 --> 22:03.739
Hey, I can see some
of her Papa's features there too.

22:03.822 --> 22:06.283
Can you tell me
what brings you here, Bo-mi?

22:06.366 --> 22:08.535
- Your Papa, huh?
- No, she's here for her school.

22:08.618 --> 22:11.872
- Oh, a field trip.
- Mm. So, uh, do you like science?

22:11.955 --> 22:13.540
Yes, I do.

22:13.623 --> 22:14.958
How did you know?

22:15.876 --> 22:17.502
I heard students who come to our office

22:17.586 --> 22:21.256
are looking for experience in fields
they like for their school records.

22:21.340 --> 22:22.382
- I see.
- Oh.

22:22.466 --> 22:24.426
You not only resemble your dad,

22:24.509 --> 22:26.511
I'd say you've got
a science mind too, huh?

22:26.595 --> 22:28.638
- Oh?
- You don't know?

22:28.722 --> 22:30.932
Your Pa's the best meteorologist in Korea.

22:31.016 --> 22:32.726
Oh, come on. That's not true.

22:32.809 --> 22:35.520
You are the best.

22:36.897 --> 22:38.815
Bo-mi, here, try. Try this.

22:39.441 --> 22:42.152
Aw, look at Mr. Um.

22:42.235 --> 22:43.737
I didn't know you had a soft side.

22:43.820 --> 22:45.947
You're a real tiger in the situation room.

22:46.031 --> 22:48.158
You're a lucky girl.

22:50.911 --> 22:51.995
Mr. Um, sir.

22:52.079 --> 22:54.039
Could I have a piece
of your sausage as well?

22:54.122 --> 22:55.374
- What's this?
- Hmm?

22:55.457 --> 22:56.750
Can I?

22:57.417 --> 22:59.378
You can perfectly well
get your own sausage.

22:59.461 --> 23:00.379
Yup.

23:00.462 --> 23:02.339
Bo-mi, try.

23:03.924 --> 23:04.966
Go on.

23:15.435 --> 23:17.437
- It's good, right?
- You like it?

23:22.776 --> 23:24.027
Mm.

23:25.237 --> 23:26.405
Just a moment. Sorry.

23:26.488 --> 23:27.823
- Okay.
- Mm-hmm.

23:29.991 --> 23:30.867
Eommoni.

23:30.951 --> 23:33.328
You need
to pick up the kids a little early today.

23:33.412 --> 23:34.246
Huh?

23:34.329 --> 23:35.997
Maybe it's because of the hot weather.

23:36.081 --> 23:39.501
And my eyes hurt.
And I'm not feeling so great.

23:39.584 --> 23:42.045
Ah. Well, I'm sorry.

23:42.129 --> 23:45.841
We have a dinner with our, uh, department.

23:45.924 --> 23:48.301
One of the forecasters
is going to Jeju.

23:48.927 --> 23:51.721
The director herself arranged it,
so it'd be really hard for me

23:51.805 --> 23:52.722
to not be there.

23:52.806 --> 23:56.143
Uh, could my husband
just take the kids from you?

23:56.226 --> 23:58.145
He's studying now. You know that.

24:01.690 --> 24:05.861
Then I'll be right over
as soon as I am all through eating.

24:06.695 --> 24:08.488
Okay. Yeah.

24:12.325 --> 24:14.536
What to do?

24:14.619 --> 24:17.456
I suggested it.
I can't back out of it now.

24:27.090 --> 24:28.508
I'm not a kid.

24:28.592 --> 24:30.302
I'm a man.

24:30.385 --> 24:31.928
And in fact, I'm yours.

24:34.222 --> 24:35.765
Hey, we're at work.

24:35.849 --> 24:37.767
Then maybe you should say "Forecaster."

24:39.394 --> 24:42.355
I know you want to…
to draw some kind of boundary

24:43.190 --> 24:45.275
between professional and personal with us.

24:45.358 --> 24:47.360
I understand how you feel,

24:47.444 --> 24:50.030
and I'll do what I can
to cooperate like I said.

24:50.113 --> 24:51.198
Still…

24:53.617 --> 24:54.826
I'm Si-woo.

24:56.369 --> 24:58.705
Not Han Ki-jun who you dated before.

24:59.289 --> 25:00.415
It's Si-woo.

25:03.376 --> 25:06.046
And none of this right now
is about that man.

25:06.129 --> 25:09.424
I know what you went through with him,
how hurt you were.

25:09.508 --> 25:11.593
I know why you're so scared
of office romance,

25:11.676 --> 25:14.137
and why you're worried
about everyone finding out, okay?

25:14.221 --> 25:17.182
Still, that was that relationship.

25:17.265 --> 25:19.142
And this one is ours now.

25:20.936 --> 25:23.313
I don't want you
comparing us all the time.

25:24.564 --> 25:25.524
It doesn't feel good.

25:25.607 --> 25:28.026
When did I ever compare you to Ki-jun?

25:30.111 --> 25:34.574
The reason that you
kept me a secret at a distance,

25:34.658 --> 25:38.203
treating me like a kid is all because
of what happened with Ki-jun, okay?

25:38.787 --> 25:42.457
You're afraid you might see him in me
and maybe get hurt in the same way.

25:43.041 --> 25:44.251
And get humiliated again…

25:45.460 --> 25:46.878
just like you did before.

25:47.671 --> 25:49.464
- Lee Si-woo…
- It's true.

25:49.548 --> 25:51.174
I can't consider getting married.

25:51.258 --> 25:52.968
That's just not the way I'm built.

25:53.885 --> 25:57.138
But still, I still want
to be in love with you.

25:59.641 --> 26:01.017
I really…

26:03.353 --> 26:04.938
really adore you.

26:07.148 --> 26:08.191
And…

26:10.026 --> 26:12.279
if that's confusing at all, I'm sorry.

26:14.281 --> 26:16.157
I'm asking for just your love…

26:17.284 --> 26:21.037
when there's nothing in the world
that I could bring to this.

26:23.373 --> 26:24.583
And so…

26:25.875 --> 26:28.712
I would understand
if you want to reconsider us.

26:31.214 --> 26:32.173
You can.

26:34.092 --> 26:37.220
But I can't do this casual.

26:39.514 --> 26:43.435
I can't have some moderate tepid thing
where we draw lines for each other.

26:44.019 --> 26:45.520
I really don't think I could.

26:47.147 --> 26:48.940
What are you saying right now?

26:53.820 --> 26:55.030
That you can…

26:56.573 --> 26:58.742
While I'm in Jeju, think about it.

26:59.784 --> 27:01.745
If you want to continue…

27:04.497 --> 27:05.749
or break it off.

27:34.736 --> 27:36.988
FATHER

28:02.555 --> 28:04.349
Yes, Jin Ha-kyung.

28:07.227 --> 28:09.729
I'll look into that
and follow it up. Thank you.

28:09.813 --> 28:10.689
Okay.

28:13.316 --> 28:16.111
KMA HEAT WAVE FORECAST

28:19.197 --> 28:21.449
THE WORST HEAT WAVE EVER!
THERE'S NO END TO IT

28:21.533 --> 28:23.702
PEOPLE ARE GROWING TIRED
OF THE MURDEROUS HEAT

28:28.540 --> 28:29.999
My god! This is ridiculous.

28:31.626 --> 28:34.629
A treat.
Thanks to lovely Bo-mi. Thank you.

28:37.632 --> 28:39.467
Oh, Bo-mi's not here?

28:39.551 --> 28:40.802
- In the restroom.
- Oh.

28:40.885 --> 28:42.345
- Go ahead. Get a drink.
- On you?

28:42.429 --> 28:43.763
- Mm-hmm.
- I'll get that one, then.

28:45.348 --> 28:46.975
- Is it good?
- Mm-hmm.

29:29.309 --> 29:31.519
PETITION FOR DIVORCE

30:11.226 --> 30:12.477
Oh, gosh!

30:12.560 --> 30:14.729
Honey! Honey, are you okay?

30:14.813 --> 30:18.691
Appa. My father, please.

30:19.526 --> 30:20.693
Oh, my god.

30:20.777 --> 30:22.195
- She's lucky.
- It is luck.

30:22.278 --> 30:25.323
- Oh, I'm fair pretty too.
- If I just got her skin…

30:25.406 --> 30:26.616
Did you have lunch?

30:26.699 --> 30:27.909
- Yeah.
- Oh, Forecaster.

30:27.992 --> 30:31.246
Hey! Someone, please help!
A student collapsed over here!

30:31.788 --> 30:33.498
A student's in there,
on the floor in the bathroom,

30:33.581 --> 30:34.874
- and she's choking.
- Um Bo-mi.

30:35.834 --> 30:37.502
Oh, my!

30:37.585 --> 30:40.213
- Hey! Call 119! 119! Hurry!
- Okay.

30:45.426 --> 30:48.471
EMERGENCY CENTER

30:49.138 --> 30:50.849
- Hey.
- What's going on? Where is she?

30:50.932 --> 30:52.851
I don't know what…

30:53.434 --> 30:55.895
She was fine when we were having lunch,

30:55.979 --> 30:57.730
but she collapsed
in the bathroom right after.

30:57.814 --> 30:59.816
She couldn't breathe
and had a terrible sort of rash

30:59.899 --> 31:02.318
- on her whole neck that went down.
- And what did you feed her?

31:02.402 --> 31:03.862
She ate at the cafeteria.

31:03.945 --> 31:05.446
What was the food there, though?

31:07.323 --> 31:12.620
Uh, there was rice, seaweed,
and radish, pork sausage, and soup.

31:12.704 --> 31:14.163
You gave pork to our daughter?

31:14.747 --> 31:15.582
Yeah.

31:15.665 --> 31:18.084
Bo-mi has always been allergic to that.

31:18.751 --> 31:19.961
Did you forget?

31:21.588 --> 31:23.715
Bo-mi, here. Try this.

31:32.348 --> 31:33.683
- It's good, right?
- You like it?

31:37.020 --> 31:38.897
I can't believe you.

31:56.748 --> 32:00.710
"The worst heat yet! No end in sight.
Murder by heat in Korea."

32:01.377 --> 32:04.005
I told you not to let them
get so sensational.

32:07.050 --> 32:08.468
Han Ki-jun, listen!

32:09.052 --> 32:10.553
Yu-jin has left.

32:11.137 --> 32:12.013
What?

32:12.096 --> 32:13.806
She wants to live alone.

32:15.767 --> 32:16.768
Why?

32:20.104 --> 32:21.940
What am I supposed to do now, Ha-kyung?

32:44.295 --> 32:45.588
Hey, Mom.

32:46.214 --> 32:48.716
How are you? Everything good?

32:51.511 --> 32:54.180
No, I just miss you,
and I wanted to hear your voice.

32:57.642 --> 32:59.143
Yeah, he's doing well, of course.

33:01.813 --> 33:03.940
She doesn't pick up the phone.

33:04.023 --> 33:06.150
And she doesn't read my texts.

33:06.734 --> 33:08.319
How did this happen?

33:09.112 --> 33:11.948
Is it 'cause of her living with her ex?

33:16.035 --> 33:17.996
Uh, or did something else go down?

33:18.079 --> 33:19.205
Hey.

33:20.206 --> 33:22.834
Did you know that when we dated,

33:22.917 --> 33:27.130
I felt like your work was a whole lot
more important than me, you know?

33:28.965 --> 33:31.259
Every time I felt that way, I got sad

33:31.342 --> 33:33.928
because I felt like
I would always be your second.

33:35.013 --> 33:38.266
At the same time, I couldn't help
but feel like I was small and juvenile

33:38.349 --> 33:39.684
for having all of those thoughts.

33:42.895 --> 33:43.938
I did that to you?

33:44.689 --> 33:45.732
Mm-hmm.

33:46.733 --> 33:47.567
You did.

33:48.693 --> 33:51.904
You're very authoritative when you say
you need to focus on your work life.

33:53.823 --> 33:56.451
Of course, you said that to me
as a deputy director.

33:56.534 --> 33:58.369
Still, I was your boyfriend first.

33:59.579 --> 34:01.914
I felt awful so many times 'cause of that.

34:03.833 --> 34:09.213
I know you want to draw a boundary
between professional and personal with us.

34:09.297 --> 34:11.299
I understand how you feel,

34:11.382 --> 34:13.968
and I'll do what I can
to cooperate like I said.

34:14.052 --> 34:14.927
Still…

34:15.928 --> 34:17.221
But…

34:20.308 --> 34:23.895
One day, I realized that
I was doing the same thing to Yu-jin.

34:25.188 --> 34:28.399
I was comparing her to you
over every little thing.

34:29.358 --> 34:31.069
That was that relationship.

34:31.152 --> 34:32.820
And this one is ours now.

34:33.404 --> 34:35.490
I don't want you comparing us
all the time.

34:36.991 --> 34:38.326
It doesn't feel good.

34:41.287 --> 34:44.248
Yu-jin is just Yu-jin.

34:45.666 --> 34:47.043
I'm Si-woo.

34:47.126 --> 34:49.170
Not Han Ki-jun who you dated before.

34:49.253 --> 34:50.755
It's Si-woo.

34:50.838 --> 34:53.424
And none of this right now
is about that man.

35:07.730 --> 35:09.690
Don't worry.
I took care of everything.

35:10.900 --> 35:13.027
Yeah. Ah, you're here.

35:13.111 --> 35:14.904
Mr. Um's daughter is okay.

35:15.488 --> 35:17.907
It looks like she made it through
the worst of it. She'll be all right.

35:18.699 --> 35:19.826
That's good.

35:20.701 --> 35:22.078
Uh, about our team dinner--

35:22.161 --> 35:24.914
Forecaster Lee is gonna meet us
straight at the restaurant.

35:24.997 --> 35:28.334
And Mr. Um will join us if the situation
with his daughter improves enough.

35:29.877 --> 35:30.837
Right.

35:47.353 --> 35:48.729
Here. Have this.

35:49.564 --> 35:50.690
Oh, thank you.

35:58.072 --> 36:00.533
Studying was the easiest thing
for me to do.

36:02.702 --> 36:05.913
I knew what I had to do
to get good grades.

36:07.957 --> 36:10.877
But this damn weather and family, though,

36:10.960 --> 36:13.254
I have no idea
how to wrap my head around it.

36:14.630 --> 36:17.508
There's no equation, manual.

36:19.010 --> 36:21.554
I never learned how to be a good father.

36:22.972 --> 36:25.725
I don't have the smallest idea…

36:26.350 --> 36:28.102
how to be a good husband or dad.

36:32.064 --> 36:34.066
The fact that you worry about all that…

36:34.775 --> 36:36.235
means you are one already.

36:39.030 --> 36:39.864
You know,

36:41.073 --> 36:45.453
I've never once seen my dad
think about any of that stuff.

36:50.124 --> 36:52.668
Just putting that out there.

37:03.679 --> 37:04.722
How's Bo-mi?

37:06.265 --> 37:07.350
She's better now.

37:07.850 --> 37:10.436
She'll have
to be discharged late tonight

37:11.354 --> 37:13.564
when the sedative they had
to give her has worn off.

37:14.398 --> 37:15.858
You should get going.

37:18.402 --> 37:20.655
I thought her dermatitis had improved.

37:24.700 --> 37:27.203
How many diseases in the world
just go away on their own?

37:28.371 --> 37:32.166
She stays well because of
the protection I provide her.

37:32.250 --> 37:34.585
What she eats, where she sleeps,
the clothes she wears.

37:37.088 --> 37:38.130
I'm sorry.

37:38.756 --> 37:39.632
For what?

37:39.715 --> 37:41.550
'Cause I almost killed her,

37:41.634 --> 37:44.387
pretending to be a good dad
and knowing nothing.

37:45.680 --> 37:46.931
How could you know…

37:49.267 --> 37:51.936
enough to be able to even pretend?

38:15.835 --> 38:17.753
- Are you going out?
- Huh?

38:17.837 --> 38:20.548
Yeah. I have a research interview.

38:21.132 --> 38:22.341
Where are you going?

38:22.925 --> 38:24.427
Where do you have to go at night?

38:25.261 --> 38:27.013
You're not going to Ha-kyung's again.

38:27.096 --> 38:29.682
You think Ha-kyung's
the only thing important in my life?

38:30.391 --> 38:31.726
Well, sort of.

38:32.852 --> 38:33.853
Don't be late.

38:34.520 --> 38:36.105
And don't drink too much either.

38:43.321 --> 38:45.698
MOTHER-IN-LAW

38:54.832 --> 38:57.251
- Are you sure you're okay?
- Hmm? Why?

38:57.835 --> 39:00.546
Your mother-in-law called.
She's been calling for a while now.

39:01.714 --> 39:05.259
If it's really so bad,
then she can call her own son.

39:05.885 --> 39:07.553
You know he's studying.

39:07.636 --> 39:11.474
Yes. And here I am
working to support him too.

39:11.557 --> 39:14.602
From time to time,
I need a little chance to breathe.

39:15.227 --> 39:16.979
I'm going to enjoy the food tonight.

39:17.063 --> 39:19.732
I'll eat and drink and noraebang later?

39:22.443 --> 39:25.237
Oh, uh, Mr. Shin. So what's he up to?

39:25.321 --> 39:27.365
Normally, he works and goes home.

39:27.948 --> 39:28.908
A new girlfriend?

39:29.867 --> 39:32.370
Ah, you know, he should
be dating at his age.

39:32.453 --> 39:33.788
Mm.

39:34.997 --> 39:37.458
- Director. Over here.
- Here.

39:38.292 --> 39:39.251
Oh.

39:46.801 --> 39:51.389
I can see that you've worked very hard
on these drawings.

39:51.472 --> 39:53.808
It's good for nothing.

39:53.891 --> 39:56.936
I don't even know
where I should go with all of it.

39:59.355 --> 40:01.148
Why did you choose the penguin?

40:02.441 --> 40:03.526
They're cute. Why not?

40:03.609 --> 40:05.444
In what way are they cute?

40:05.528 --> 40:07.029
Hmm…

40:07.113 --> 40:11.575
Well, I think about the way they walk,
it's adorable.

40:12.368 --> 40:16.664
Waddle, waddle.

40:18.833 --> 40:23.796
They, um, don't walk
that way to look cute.

40:24.505 --> 40:25.506
Sorry?

40:26.465 --> 40:31.637
Um, penguins waddle
'cause their ambulation is…

40:31.720 --> 40:34.557
They follow a pendulum system.

40:34.640 --> 40:38.310
If a pendulum reaches
its peak on one side,

40:38.394 --> 40:42.690
it pauses for a moment for the energy
to change from potential back to kinetic.

40:44.150 --> 40:46.610
Uh… Yeah.

40:46.694 --> 40:47.987
Oh…

40:48.612 --> 40:51.699
I had no idea. Okay. So?

40:52.241 --> 40:53.075
Uh…

40:53.742 --> 40:54.827
So?

40:55.703 --> 40:57.413
Uh…

40:58.831 --> 41:01.417
- When the penguin waddles like that…
- Uh-huh.

41:01.500 --> 41:04.795
…it can save up to 80 percent
of the energy it needs.

41:04.879 --> 41:06.172
Mm, save energy.

41:07.840 --> 41:13.387
So, uh, the really cool thing
about them is this real efficiency.

41:13.471 --> 41:16.807
Oh, really? Hmm.

41:16.891 --> 41:20.394
Eighty percent…

41:23.397 --> 41:24.815
Uh, also…

41:25.566 --> 41:28.736
the penguins' blood vessels
are wrapped in a very unique pattern.

41:28.819 --> 41:30.029
The "wonder net."

41:30.112 --> 41:33.073
The veins and arteries
are all intertwined, so…

41:33.157 --> 41:35.993
Whoa, you really know a lot.

41:36.577 --> 41:39.246
You are a zoologist!

41:39.330 --> 41:40.372
No, no.

41:46.921 --> 41:48.422
Everyone's taking their time, huh?

41:48.506 --> 41:51.050
Yeah, they all said
they would run a little late.

41:51.759 --> 41:56.680
Maybe we should order something first?
Here, Director. We're all hungry.

41:56.764 --> 42:00.976
- Oh, no. You, Ms. Oh.
- Ah, um, what should we order?

42:01.060 --> 42:03.354
Let's start
with some pork belly. Yeah.

42:03.437 --> 42:05.564
Hmm, that okay, Director?

42:19.537 --> 42:20.371
Ooh.

42:27.920 --> 42:31.131
Go ahead. You young people
love this kind of thing.

42:31.215 --> 42:32.550
Oh, okay.

42:32.633 --> 42:35.636
Uh, why did you want
to meet all of a sudden?

42:35.719 --> 42:38.180
Let's eat first, and then we'll talk.

42:38.264 --> 42:39.723
Uh…

42:40.349 --> 42:41.559
Ooh.

42:48.524 --> 42:49.525
Uh…

42:50.526 --> 42:52.736
How's Ha-kyung doing now?

42:54.154 --> 42:58.158
She's swamped with work
because of the heat wave.

42:59.326 --> 43:02.705
She hasn't said anything
since my last visit with her, though?

43:02.788 --> 43:05.249
No. Not really. No.

43:07.543 --> 43:09.253
I was so off guard.

43:10.713 --> 43:13.007
She threw the not-getting-married thing
at me,

43:13.090 --> 43:17.636
and I was mortified, I had to back off,
and let it all just go.

43:18.596 --> 43:22.141
Ah, you know, the one who lives upstairs--

43:22.224 --> 43:24.602
Not Seok-ho, not that man.

43:24.685 --> 43:25.728
Why?

43:25.811 --> 43:27.271
He's not right for the Director.

43:27.354 --> 43:30.232
Their personalities, tastes,
hobbies, lifestyles,

43:30.316 --> 43:32.151
nothing in common at all.

43:32.818 --> 43:34.403
I can say that for sure.

43:34.486 --> 43:37.448
Ah, but they can find those things
when they're together.

43:38.115 --> 43:40.451
To put it bluntly,
they're two different people,

43:40.534 --> 43:42.328
two different lives, two sets of parents.

43:42.411 --> 43:45.539
I mean, how can everything
be perfect from the beginning?

43:46.373 --> 43:48.751
It would be weird
if there were no differences.

43:50.961 --> 43:53.130
You… have a point.

43:53.213 --> 43:58.302
You see, marriage isn't about
a couple perfectly coming together.

43:58.886 --> 44:03.432
The joining comes first,
so they can perfect each other, huh?

44:04.350 --> 44:09.772
This process is what married life is for,
so at the end of that is a good couple.

44:11.065 --> 44:15.277
Young people these days think
that it's some kind of insurance plan

44:15.361 --> 44:17.863
or just some sort of big legal headache.

44:17.946 --> 44:19.823
That's why most won't even give it a try.

44:19.907 --> 44:24.119
They're busy calculating
all the conditions and the concerns.

44:24.870 --> 44:27.623
You've never regretted yours, then?

44:28.415 --> 44:29.416
What?

44:29.500 --> 44:31.543
Your own marriage, you know?

44:34.546 --> 44:35.839
Well, uh…

44:35.923 --> 44:37.758
I've always regretted it.

44:37.841 --> 44:41.428
I've said that he's my worst enemy
and I hope lightning kills him.

44:42.096 --> 44:43.138
But…

44:43.681 --> 44:46.475
if someone asks me if I would do it again,

44:47.267 --> 44:51.397
if I could somehow go back in time,
well, I'd probably say yes.

44:52.189 --> 44:53.399
Why?

44:55.234 --> 44:58.278
Through it all, we had
some pretty good times, him and I, too.

44:58.362 --> 45:00.698
Especially with Tae-kyung and Ha-kyung.

45:00.781 --> 45:05.911
And those girls are the finest works
I've ever created.

45:10.082 --> 45:14.795
- So what I want to say to you is--
- But still, I really mean it.

45:14.878 --> 45:17.297
Not Seok-ho. Not with Ha-kyung.

45:18.090 --> 45:19.341
Not ever.

45:20.008 --> 45:21.885
Why are you being so obstinate?

45:21.969 --> 45:23.137
Who are you to say?

45:27.683 --> 45:29.727
Oh, the pizza is getting cold, ma'am.

45:29.810 --> 45:32.646
Please. I'll grab you a slice.

45:44.366 --> 45:45.492
Mm.

46:05.179 --> 46:07.347
Looks like our dinner's not working out.

46:07.431 --> 46:08.265
What do you mean?

46:08.348 --> 46:11.268
We're having it right now.
Quite deliciously, I might add.

46:12.060 --> 46:15.731
Mrs. Oh, looks like you forgot
why you called for this event.

46:15.814 --> 46:17.775
First, it's to say goodbye
to Forecaster Lee.

46:17.858 --> 46:20.736
Second, it's supposed to be
the first ever get-together

46:20.819 --> 46:22.529
of our current team, isn't it?

46:23.614 --> 46:25.449
Well, what can we do now?

46:25.949 --> 46:27.826
They're not gonna show up.

46:28.869 --> 46:30.704
It's their loss if they're not here.

46:31.205 --> 46:33.499
Even though the Director herself
put it together.

46:33.582 --> 46:35.083
We can't control them.

46:36.752 --> 46:38.337
Everything is what it is.

46:38.921 --> 46:40.798
So let's get two more orders.

46:41.465 --> 46:43.050
We'll rename this night

46:43.133 --> 46:46.762
as a well-deserved retreat
just for the women of Team Two.

46:46.845 --> 46:48.764
Do you approve, Director?

46:48.847 --> 46:50.098
What do you say?

46:50.933 --> 46:51.850
Okay.

46:51.934 --> 46:54.895
A women's retreat sounds great.

46:54.978 --> 46:57.314
Sir, could we please get
two more pork belly orders?

46:57.397 --> 46:59.525
- Soju too.
- You got it.

46:59.608 --> 47:00.692
We're ordering some soju?

47:00.776 --> 47:03.278
Well, now that we've re-christened
our night, we might as well.

47:03.362 --> 47:05.072
- Ooh!
- How's that sound?

47:05.697 --> 47:07.157
Mm, thanks.

47:11.286 --> 47:13.288
Oh, wow. Oh, wow. Oh, wow.

47:16.792 --> 47:19.086
- Here you go.
- Oh, yes. All right.

47:22.464 --> 47:24.299
- Noraebang later?
- Well, of course!

47:24.383 --> 47:25.801
- Of course.
- Yay!

47:25.884 --> 47:26.969
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

47:27.052 --> 47:27.970
Cheers.

47:28.053 --> 47:31.682
- Let's go. Let's go.
- Let's go. This place!

47:34.309 --> 47:36.645
Do we have to go in here?
I have to go home.

47:36.728 --> 47:39.147
- Hey! Why are you going home?
- Let's barbecue now!

47:39.231 --> 47:41.817
- You are such a good singer.
- Come on. Just one more.

47:41.900 --> 47:44.444
I'm a high soprano.

47:44.528 --> 47:47.823
- High soprano.
- I don't think their songs in low keys

47:47.906 --> 47:49.366
are real songs.

47:50.492 --> 47:52.327
I'm a baritone.

48:04.339 --> 48:06.383
DIRECTOR JIN HA-KYUNG

48:28.614 --> 48:29.823
Yes, Ms. Oh.

48:32.576 --> 48:33.785
Where are you right now?

48:38.165 --> 48:41.084
The Director is so drunk.

48:41.168 --> 48:43.170
I have to go home now.

48:43.253 --> 48:46.548
I'm sorry but can you come
pick her up, Forecaster Lee?

48:53.972 --> 48:55.223
I'm here.

48:59.519 --> 49:00.812
How drunk are you?

49:03.148 --> 49:04.399
Can you walk on your own?

49:15.494 --> 49:17.704
I want things to work out.

49:19.790 --> 49:23.126
I want things to work out
for the two of us.

49:28.590 --> 49:29.716
But…

49:31.802 --> 49:33.387
that's the only thing.

49:35.931 --> 49:41.436
A love that stays under control
with tempered feelings.

49:41.520 --> 49:43.730
I like it simple and stable.

49:45.482 --> 49:48.235
If things start to go beyond moderate…

49:50.529 --> 49:52.364
I become anxious.

49:55.867 --> 49:57.327
Then I feel…

49:58.370 --> 50:01.415
I become someone else and not myself.

50:06.044 --> 50:07.546
So all I can do…

50:09.464 --> 50:11.258
is do it moderately.

50:14.928 --> 50:16.555
Get up. Let's take you back home.

50:18.015 --> 50:19.975
So then you should decide.

50:21.518 --> 50:23.937
You should decide while you're in Jeju.

50:29.609 --> 50:33.697
If you think you can do it
moderately or not.

50:34.197 --> 50:36.658
Really think about it then decide.

50:42.205 --> 50:44.791
One of my superiors once told me…

50:46.293 --> 50:48.336
that when I don't understand
a satellite image,

50:48.420 --> 50:50.756
no matter how long I've looked at it,

50:50.839 --> 50:56.803
I should stand a little further away
and observe the flow of the clouds."

51:19.910 --> 51:23.872
To be honest, I didn't understand
what he said at the time.

51:23.955 --> 51:27.667
I've never seen a satellite image
I didn't understand back then,

51:27.751 --> 51:30.962
and I was very confident
about everything related to weather.

51:36.301 --> 51:37.344
Then…

51:38.428 --> 51:39.554
I met you.

52:11.044 --> 52:13.004
Oh, my head.

52:21.304 --> 52:23.473
Oh.

52:41.032 --> 52:43.952
Oh, you're flying right after work?

52:45.537 --> 52:46.580
That's my stuff.

52:46.663 --> 52:47.747
Oh, you scared me.

52:51.001 --> 52:53.920
Uh, are you moving home?

52:54.004 --> 52:56.131
No. I was thinking I would stay
at the office again

52:56.214 --> 52:58.049
since it's typhoon season, you know.

52:59.426 --> 53:00.510
Where is Lee Si-woo?

53:01.094 --> 53:02.304
Si-woo left.

53:02.387 --> 53:03.513
Sorry?

53:03.597 --> 53:07.267
Jeju. He left today. You didn't know?

53:09.436 --> 53:12.939
Anyway, soup over there
to nurse your head.

53:39.007 --> 53:40.217
Did you know

53:40.884 --> 53:44.429
you were the strangest weather
I've ever seen in my life?

53:56.691 --> 53:58.485
Uh…

53:59.486 --> 54:00.654
There was an accident? Where?

54:00.737 --> 54:02.113
Where and how bad is it?

54:02.197 --> 54:03.198
I…

54:03.907 --> 54:05.200
Hold on a moment. Who is this?

54:05.283 --> 54:06.910
If you tell me
which hospital it is, I'll--

54:06.993 --> 54:08.328
This is Chae Yu-jin.

54:15.460 --> 54:17.170
I'm with Si-woo right now.

54:45.657 --> 54:46.574
Hello?

54:47.784 --> 54:49.244
Why are you calling me so late?

54:51.788 --> 54:53.164
Wait, what's that?

54:56.626 --> 54:59.421
Ha-kyung. What the hell's going on?

55:00.005 --> 55:01.464
Lee Si-woo is hurt.

55:01.548 --> 55:02.757
Okay, I get Lee Si-woo is hurt.

55:02.841 --> 55:05.176
But why on earth
is he there right now with Yu-jin?

55:05.760 --> 55:07.512
- Coincidence.
- What?

55:08.638 --> 55:10.598
In Jeju, they ran into each other.

55:14.769 --> 55:16.646
EMERGENCY MEDICAL CENTER

55:35.832 --> 55:37.208
Lee Si-woo.

55:44.341 --> 55:46.051
This is all your fault.

55:46.634 --> 55:47.969
How is this my fault?

55:48.053 --> 55:51.097
I was so scared
of an office romance because of you,

55:51.181 --> 55:54.184
that I was always on edge
with Si-woo and so afraid.

55:54.768 --> 55:59.314
Uh, you were always on edge
and scared even when you were with me.

55:59.397 --> 56:01.816
I was scared of you!

56:02.650 --> 56:07.530
I was so consumed
by the fear of getting hurt.

56:07.614 --> 56:11.409
Now that I never told him
how I really felt.

56:11.493 --> 56:13.370
Or did anything.

56:17.165 --> 56:19.084
Now what do I do?

56:19.667 --> 56:21.169
What do I do?

56:22.504 --> 56:25.048
What do I do now?

56:34.599 --> 56:37.519
So it wasn't because
of Lee Si-woo's principle

56:37.602 --> 56:39.687
of not wanting to get married.

56:40.605 --> 56:43.316
I was scared that it would get too hot,

56:43.400 --> 56:45.860
too hot to the point
where I can't control it.

56:46.444 --> 56:51.533
I was afraid to lose control
of my emotions, so I was making excuses

56:52.826 --> 56:57.122
to stop the last one degree from rising
to reach the boiling point.

56:58.123 --> 56:59.207
But…

57:06.089 --> 57:08.216
- Mr. Um.
- Hmm?

57:13.179 --> 57:16.850
- Wow. When did that start, huh?
- Oh!

57:27.068 --> 57:29.320
Hello. Headquarters. This is Um.

57:30.405 --> 57:31.698
Yeah. We just saw it.

57:32.198 --> 57:33.324
It is a…

57:33.825 --> 57:34.742
Typhoon, yes.

57:34.826 --> 57:37.662
Number 15 Elisha
that was following Number 14 Ricky.

57:38.413 --> 57:41.291
Around eleven o'clock today,
it was moving northeastward,

57:41.374 --> 57:43.126
300km near Okinawa.

57:43.209 --> 57:46.296
The central pressure was 990,
max wind velocity 20 per second,

57:46.379 --> 57:48.006
and a radius of 150.

57:48.089 --> 57:49.507
- That's it.
- Can I have that?

57:50.550 --> 57:52.177
NATIONAL TYPHOON CENTER

57:52.260 --> 57:54.929
Satellite Center. Can you check
the intensity of the typhoon?

57:55.013 --> 57:59.601
At 10:00 p.m., we're looking at a path
straight for the southern Jeju Sea,

57:59.684 --> 58:03.229
120km over the western sea near Okinawa.

58:03.313 --> 58:06.733
980 central pressure,
max velocity, 28, strong wind, 200.

58:08.818 --> 58:11.279
Mm, I understand.

58:11.362 --> 58:14.824
Keep sending us the data. Mm-hmm.

58:15.408 --> 58:16.284
- Mr. Shin.
- Yes?

58:16.367 --> 58:18.244
Give me data on ocean heat change
by time period.

58:18.328 --> 58:19.370
- Yes, sir.
- Ms. Oh.

58:19.454 --> 58:20.747
Figure out steering current flow

58:20.830 --> 58:22.874
and the vertical wind sheer
from the updated forecast.

58:22.957 --> 58:24.209
Yes, sir.

58:24.292 --> 58:25.376
VERTICAL WIND SHEAR:
CHANGE IN WINDSPEED WITH HEIGHT

58:25.460 --> 58:26.836
STEERING FLOW: THE FLOW
THAT INFLUENCES TYPHOON MOVEMENT

58:55.990 --> 58:59.369
You're all dead, all of you.

59:44.289 --> 59:49.419
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

01:00:27.206 --> 01:00:29.459
I didn't realize
you were so invested.

01:00:30.001 --> 01:00:33.796
Who knows what I feel?
It seems like everything's falling apart.

01:00:33.880 --> 01:00:35.298
I want to talk to the guy in charge.

01:00:35.381 --> 01:00:37.091
- I can't calm down!
- What's going on?

01:00:37.175 --> 01:00:38.968
What you're doing
is obstructing official duties.

01:00:39.052 --> 01:00:40.928
It's important
that they can do their work.

01:00:41.721 --> 01:00:45.975
No. No more. Just be
a decent man for once and sign it.

01:00:46.559 --> 01:00:48.811
Except Yu-jin left me now, so…

01:00:48.895 --> 01:00:50.271
Can you let me go?

01:00:50.355 --> 01:00:53.024
Is there any way
I could come along to Jeju Island?

01:00:53.107 --> 01:00:56.653
There's so much that we expect
people we love to figure out.

01:00:56.736 --> 01:00:59.906
But what if we took nothing for granted

01:00:59.989 --> 01:01:01.783
- and said everything explicitly?
- Yu-jin.

01:01:01.866 --> 01:01:04.952
All I really wanted was time
to realign and be together.

01:01:05.536 --> 01:01:07.622
I must have missed where we fell out.
